<section class="section prose-grid" id="making"><h2>From implementation<br/>to evidence.</h2><div><h3>Human direction, agent implementation</h3><p>The design, atmosphere, pacing, and release decisions remained human responsibilities. Agents supported implementation, iteration, and regression work inside a structured development process.</p><h3>Test the running game</h3><p>The project’s player harness sends inputs into a debug build and records screenshots and visible text. Build-bound receipts connect test evidence to the artifact being reviewed. Regression harnesses cover specific behavior; hands-on playtests judge timing, clarity, and feel.</p><h3>What the process taught</h3><p>An input being delivered does not prove the game responded correctly. The harness explicitly separates delivery from verification. That distinction, along with isolated runs and independent review, became part of the wider development system.</p><a class="text-link" href="/harness/">Explore the Godot development harness →</a></div></section></Portfolio>
